      "description": "Changes / Files / Terminal switch in the session header; selecting the active pane returns to Chat.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-seg\"><button class=\"is-active\">Changes</button><button>Files</button><button>Terminal</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-seg{display:inline-flex;gap:2px;padding:2px;border:1px solid #313338;border-radius:7px}.ds-seg button{height:24px;padding:0 8px;border:none;border-radius:6px;background:transparent;color:#aaa9a3;font:500 12.5px 'Libre Franklin',sans-serif;cursor:pointer}.ds-seg button:hover{background:#27292c;color:#eceae5}.ds-seg button.is-active{background:#2b2d31;color:#eceae5}.ds-seg button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #93b5e9}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Card Catalog",
    "overview": "xd is a library card catalog for agent sessions. Projects are drawers, sessions are index cards, and a small metal signal tab clipped to the top edge of a card says what its agent is doing. One catalog sidebar on the left holds every drawer; only the current project's drawer is pulled out to show its cards, and the rest stay one line tall and show just their tabs. The centre belongs to the session's transcript, and the right dock holds Changes, Files, Terminal and Browser.\n\nThe material is a cool graphite cabinet with bone card-stock ink in Dark, and white card stock with near-black ink in Light. Each card has one thin red ruled line under its title, the only decorative mark in the system. Colour is mostly reserved for state: green, amber and blue live on the signal tabs and the words beside them, and the chrome around them stays neutral so the agent's output stays the content. Density is that of a working tool: 12.5 to 13px UI text, 30px controls, 56px cards.\n\nAndroid follows the same world inside Material 3. Material owns the structure (navigation bar, dialogs, extended FAB, ripples, touch targets). The brand comes through as complete colour roles, Libre Franklin across the type scale, and the same drawer, card, rule and tab shapes.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Two themes only, Dark and Light. Saved names of retired themes (warm, nord, dracula) load as Dark.",
      "Session state shows through the tab's shape as well as its hue, so it still reads in grayscale.",
      "The current drawer is the only one that lifts. The current project's name sits in an outlined label frame.",
      "Every session card has one fixed height and baseline (56px on desktop).",
      "Flat, tonal surfaces. Only floating popovers and menus get a soft shadow.",
      "Drawn 24-grid stroke icons with a 2px stroke, tinted to the text around them."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Amber Rule",
        "body": "Amber means one thing: an agent is waiting on the user. No warning, badge, highlight or brand mark may use it.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Shape-Before-Hue Rule",
        "body": "A signal always has its own shape as well as its own colour. Working is a solid flag, Waiting is a taller solid flag, Done is a hollow flag, and Idle has no tab at all. A new signal surface must stay legible in grayscale.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Four States Rule",
        "body": "A session can be Idle, Working, Waiting or Done. Nothing else. There is no failed or queued session state, and cards never show one. A failed tool run is stamped in the transcript instead.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Machine Text Rule",
        "body": "JetBrains Mono is for text a machine wrote or reads: code, terminal, tool output, branch names, counts and agent wire names. Prose and chrome are always Libre Franklin.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Lift-By-Contrast Rule",
        "body": "In-flow surfaces never cast shadows. A drawer, card or panel shows that it is raised through fill and seam alone.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do take every colour from the `ThemeColors` roles (desktop) or `minimalColors` / `XdSignals` (Android), and define each new role for both Dark and Light.",
      "Do give every new session-state surface a shape difference as well as a hue difference, following the signal tab.",
      "Do keep session cards at one fixed height (56px) with the 1px ruled-red line under the title.",
      "Do keep primary actions to one per region: a bone fill with ink text in Dark, an ink fill with white text in Light.",
      "Do stamp a failed tool run in the transcript in danger red, and leave the session card's state alone.",
      "Do use drawn 24-grid, 2px stroke icons tinted to the surrounding text.",
      "Do let Material 3 own the structure on Android, and carry the brand through colour roles, Libre Franklin and the catalog shapes."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use signal amber for anything except an agent waiting on the user.",
      "Don't add a failed, queued or error state to session cards or signal tabs.",
      "Don't add a third theme or per-user accent colours. There are exactly two themes, Dark and Light.",
      "Don't bind a keyboard shortcut to Find in the catalog. Ctrl-K belongs to the terminals.",
      "Don't cast shadows from in-flow surfaces. Only floating popovers and menus get the floating-layer shadow.",
      "Don't use the ruled red for errors or emphasis. It is only the card's rule line.",
      "Don't set prose or chrome in JetBrains Mono, or fall back to the host's `monospace`.",
      "Don't use text glyphs (←, ✕, +, a letter in a box) as icons.",
      "Don't add glow, gradients or decorative motion. The only standing animation is the Working dots."
    ]
  }
}
